unity": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Alphahorizon", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.noticer.news", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.noticer.news/transgender-paedophile-dead-nsw-jail/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Notorious \u2018transgender\u2019 paedophile found dead in Australian jail just weeks before he was set to walk free!", "last_comment_created": 1794085506306, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 15, "score_up": 361, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "A notorious \"transgender\" paedophile has been found dead in a NSW jail, just weeks before he was set to walk free despite his criminal history.", "title": "Notorious 'transgender' paedophile found dead in Australian jail"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2119171532018848169", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToZ4MYhL", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 54, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8929387, "raw_content": "", "author": "diogenesofthearch", "created": 1794089571923, "profile_picture": "fYN5qnn5z9Zd", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Marina", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/TrumpDailyPosts/status/2119171532018848169", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "The cheaters biggest error was trying to create the narrative that Republicans wouldn\u2019t turn out to vote or would vote Democrat and that would be the reason Democrats won. Neither happened. Caught red handed.", "last_comment_created": 1794093890641, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 54, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToZ3EiH8", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 376, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8928586, "raw_content": "This is from (the BRILLIANT) @TruthAnswersAll on X\n\nhttps://x.com/TruthAnswersAll/status/2118529314912125382?a=6NURk4hPMTP5KLNwDSE&s=19\n\nTHE 15% BAND\n\nLook at this chart. \n59 races. Senate and governor. \nStates ordered from reddest to bluest in 2024.\n\nThe solid lines are 2024. \nThe dashed lines are 2026. \nThe shaded bands are what moved.\n\nOne formula fits all of it:\nRepublican 2026 = 0.85 \u00d7 Trump 2024\nDemocrat 2026 = Harris 2024 + 0.15 \u00d7 Trump 2024\n\nFor every 1,000 Trump points, 850 stayed Republican. 150 landed on the Democratic side.\n\nThe numbers:\nSenate: Republicans kept ~85% of Trump\u2019s share\nGovernor: ~86%\n\nVariation explained: 88%\n\nWhat makes it strange:\nIt didn\u2019t matter how red the state was. Wyoming, Ohio, Illinois, Massachusetts: same 15% (p = 0.69). The Democratic gain was sized by Trump\u2019s vote, not Harris\u2019s. The Harris part is zero.\n\nThe 0.85 beat both standard election-swing models in every set of races.\nDrop any single state and the multiplier stays between 0.846 and 0.853.\n\nWhy seats flipped:\nAt 0.85, any state where Trump got under about 58.5% falls below 50%. Texas, Kansas, Iowa, Ohio, South Carolina, North Carolina: all under that line. All flipped.\n\nWhat this means:\nMidterms are messy. This one isn\u2019t. Two sets of races, different candidates, different campaigns, and the same 15% decrease almost everywhere.\n\nA pattern this even demands answers at the ballot level: paper ballot hand counts, poll-book check-ins against votes counted, and voter files showing who actually turned out. \n\nThe numbers raise the question. \nThe ballots can answer it.", "author": "ONAVirus", "created": 1794050894361, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "RedPillosopher1776", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "The Democrats Cheated - AND THEY FOUND THE MATHEMATICAL FORMULA! ", "last_comment_created": 1794093024132, "content": "<p>This is from (the BRILLIANT) @TruthAnswersAll on X</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://x.com/TruthAnswersAll/status/2118529314912125382?a=6NURk4hPMTP5KLNwDSE&amp;s=19\" target=\"_blank\">https://x.com/TruthAnswersAll/status/2118529314912125382?a=6NURk4hPMTP5KLNwDSE&amp;s=19</a></p>\n<p>THE 15% BAND</p>\n<p>Look at this chart.\n59 races. Senate and governor.\nStates ordered from reddest to bluest in 2024.</p>\n<p>The solid lines are 2024.\nThe dashed lines are 2026.\nThe shaded bands are what moved.</p>\n<p>One formula fits all of it:\nRepublican 2026 = 0.85 \u00d7 Trump 2024\nDemocrat 2026 = Harris 2024 + 0.15 \u00d7 Trump 2024</p>\n<p>For every 1,000 Trump points, 850 stayed Republican. 150 landed on the Democratic side.</p>\n<p>The numbers:\nSenate: Republicans kept ~85% of Trump\u2019s share\nGovernor: ~86%</p>\n<p>Variation explained: 88%</p>\n<p>What makes it strange:\nIt didn\u2019t matter how red the state was. Wyoming, Ohio, Illinois, Massachusetts: same 15% (p = 0.69). The Democratic gain was sized by Trump\u2019s vote, not Harris\u2019s. The Harris part is zero.</p>\n<p>The 0.85 beat both standard election-swing models in every set of races.\nDrop any single state and the multiplier stays between 0.846 and 0.853.</p>\n<p>Why seats flipped:\nAt 0.85, any state where Trump got under about 58.5% falls below 50%. Texas, Kansas, Iowa, Ohio, South Carolina, North Carolina: all under that line. All flipped.</p>\n<p>What this means:\nMidterms are messy. This one isn\u2019t. Two sets of races, different candidates, different campaigns, and the same 15% decrease almost everywhere.</p>\n<p>A pattern this even demands answers at the ballot level: paper ballot hand counts, poll-book check-ins against votes counted, and voter files showing who actually turned out.</p>\n<p>The numbers raise the question.\nThe ballots can answer it.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 41, "score_up": 376, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToZ3FoKu", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 144, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8928960, "raw_content": "", "author": "TRUTH_BE_OUR_DOGMA", "created": 1794069596416, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Klandathu", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/5KZFLugOgKqh.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "POTUS the midterms were stolen. deploy every soldier in the US. Kick in doors and